# Git and reviews

- Never push to `main`. Create a focused branch and open a PR against its inherited base.
- Do not merge until required checks and reviews pass and the user confirms with `Yes Merge Branch X into Branch Y`.
- One concern per PR. Do not stack a second change on the same branch.
- Commit as `area: concrete change`. Add `Closes #N` only when the user named a real issue.
- Request `@codeant-ai review` on every PR.
- Request `@coderabbitai review` only for a substantially critical change. That includes a breaking change, security fix, major architecture or protocol change, new platform support claim, or repository policy or workflow change that materially affects future work.
- CodeRabbit automatically reviews non-draft PRs whose base is `main`; draft PRs are excluded by `.coderabbit.yaml`. For other bases, keep routine reviews on CodeAnt.
- `PR Policy Check` runs from the trusted default-branch workflow definition and is separate from `CI Success`. Require it directly in branch protection; it does not run until the workflow is present on the default branch.
- After each push, request CodeAnt again on the new head. Request CodeRabbit manually for substantially critical PRs, and wait for automatic CodeRabbit review on every non-draft PR targeting `main`. Fix findings and repeat until required CI checks are green, CodeAnt approves the head, all applicable CodeRabbit reviews are complete, and no review thread remains unresolved.
- Run `npm run test:all` before you say the work is done. If the network blocks `crates.io` or the Playwright browser CDN, the vendor branch in `AGENTS.md` under Blocked sandbox toolchain gives you the toolchain, the crate registry and the browser, so run the gate instead of skipping it.
- `npm run test:rust` and the Rust stage of `npm run test:all` carry no `--ignore-rust-version`, so on the documented 1.88.0 toolchain they exit 101 before compiling. Run the vendored `cargo clippy` and `cargo test` invocations from `AGENTS.md` instead, and report the script's own exit code next to the flagged substitute. Never report the unmodified script as passing.
- Reviews run to a schedule, not to a stopwatch. After a push, request CodeAnt once on the new head and then poll: `gh pr checks`, the review comments, and the bot's own status comment. Diagnosis before any request: if the bot's last reply was a rate-limit or "already reviewed" notice, or its check is pending on the current head, wait instead of asking again.
- Back off exponentially when a bot refuses or is rate limited: start at 10 minutes and double to a 60-minute cap, and only re-request when the head has changed or the backoff has elapsed with no review for that head. Never post the same request twice inside one backoff window.
- Do not finish while an applicable review or check is still pending. Keep waiting in long polls rather than declaring the work done, and if a bot stays rate limited past the cap, record that state on the PR with what you will do next instead of firing another request.
- Read `AGENTS.md`. If `COMMIT.md` exists locally, follow it for commit wording.
